1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:04,901
The weekly shop is full of decisions you have already made.

2
00:00:04,901 --> 00:00:05,674
Which coffee?

3
00:00:05,674 --> 00:00:07,993
When is the premium worth it?

4
00:00:07,993 --> 00:00:11,858
What if your AI remembered why it got something wrong?

5
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:17,277
Meet Precedent, a household replenishment agent.

6
00:00:17,277 --> 00:00:19,028
Your shopping rules, remembered.

7
00:00:19,028 --> 00:00:22,530
Add the things you buy again and again.

8
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:28,221
The dashboard separates what is handled, what needs you, and what is blocked.

9
00:00:28,221 --> 00:00:31,286
Each decision carries the rule behind it.

10
00:00:31,286 --> 00:00:34,350
This is a demo, not a checkout.

11
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:39,283
Here is the coffee story from the recorded demo.

12
00:00:39,283 --> 00:00:44,531
A twenty-two percent price increase triggers rule two: switch to the cheaper roaster.

13
00:00:44,531 --> 00:00:48,569
But the recorded return says the beans were too acidic.

14
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:53,817
The correction becomes rule seven: pay the premium and stay with Roaster A.

15
00:00:53,817 --> 00:00:57,854
The new rule supersedes the old one, without erasing it.

16
00:00:57,854 --> 00:01:03,102
Next time the price jumps, the agent follows the correction and remembers why.

17
00:01:03,102 --> 00:01:08,350
In the same eight-item replay, routine autonomy rises from zero to eighty-six percent.

18
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:12,859
Memory also needs a way to handle disagreement.

19
00:01:12,859 --> 00:01:16,067
Rule one says to buy the house blend.

20
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:19,276
Rule eight says to hold off on beans.

21
00:01:19,276 --> 00:01:21,682
Both apply to the same restock.

22
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:24,088
Precedent pauses instead of silently guessing.

23
00:01:24,088 --> 00:01:28,099
Here is the real interface: buy it, then explain why.

24
00:01:28,099 --> 00:01:30,104
The answer becomes rule nine.

25
00:01:30,104 --> 00:01:35,719
It overrules the conflicting skip rule, while rule one stays active as supporting history.

26
00:01:35,719 --> 00:01:41,334
The basket now cites the new rule, and the audit has no unresolved conflicts.

27
00:01:41,334 --> 00:01:47,350
Learning is a visible change in the record, not a hidden change to a prompt.

28
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:52,320
The public sandbox and the mainnet record are separate.

29
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,990
Walrus Memory holds twenty recorded memories on Sui mainnet.

30
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:59,253
Tatum provides the GraphQL gateway used to check

31
00:01:59,253 --> 00:02:03,738
that the account is active and the configured delegate is registered.

32
00:02:03,738 --> 00:02:08,224
This is an actual saved result from the live proof page.

33
00:02:08,224 --> 00:02:12,710
It verifies the account and delegate, not every individual memory transaction.

34
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:18,012
The weekly shop should not require a weekly debate.

35
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:19,879
It should require a record.

36
00:02:19,879 --> 00:02:24,735
Precedent: written in your words, cited before it acts, superseded rather than erased.

37
00:02:24,735 --> 00:02:27,350
Try the demo and inspect the proof.
